<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>About Us</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('../partials/storefront-header') %>

  <main class="about-page">
    <h1>How Thrift On Works</h1>
    <p class="about-intro">
      Thrift On is an online-only thrift store with in-store pickup. Every item is
      donated, one-of-a-kind, and photographed by hand &mdash; when it's gone, it's gone.
    </p>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>1. Donations become listings</h2>
      <p>
        Every item starts as a donation. We photograph it, and an AI assistant drafts a
        title, description, and starting price &mdash; but nothing goes live until a real
        person reviews and approves it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>2. Browse and reserve online</h2>
      <p>
        Add anything you like to your cart, and it's reserved just for you &mdash; no one
        else can grab it out from under you. Check out securely online with a card, no
        in-store payment needed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>3. Prices drop the longer an item sits</h2>
      <p>
        Since every item is unique, prices gradually decrease the longer it goes
        unsold, until it's eventually retired from the shop. The best finds don't
        usually last long &mdash; but patient shoppers are sometimes rewarded.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>4. Pick up in-store</h2>
      <p>
        Once your order is confirmed, our staff pulls your items from their bins and
        has them ready and waiting for you at the counter.
      </p>
    </section>

    <a class="back-link" href="/">&larr; Back to browse</a>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
